{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_1>\nn, m = map(int, input().split())\na = [int(i) % m for i in input().split()]\n\ndef generate_subseq_sums(arr, mod):\n    res = set()\n    def dfs(idx, current_sum):\n        if idx == len(arr):\n            res.add(current_sum % mod)\n        else:\n            dfs(idx + 1, (current_sum + arr[idx]) % mod)\n            dfs(idx + 1, current_sum)\n    dfs(0, 0)\n    return res\n\nhalf = n // 2\nleft_sums = generate_subseq_sums(a[:half], m)\nright_sums = generate_subseq_sums(a[half:], m)\n\nright_sorted = sorted(right_sums)\n\nimport bisect\nmax_val = 0\nfor s in left_sums:\n    target = m - s\n    idx = bisect.bisect_left(right_sorted, target)\n    if idx > 0:\n        candidate = s + right_sorted[idx - 1]\n        if candidate > max_val:\n            max_val = candidate\n    if idx < len(right_sorted):\n        candidate = s + right_sorted[idx]\n        if candidate > max_val:\n            max_val = candidate\n\nprint(max_val)\n</your_rewritten_code_1>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <set>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cmath>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nset<int> generate_subseq_sums(const vector<int>& arr, int mod) {\n    set<int> res;\n    \n    function<void(int, int)> dfs = [&](int idx, int current_sum) {\n        if (idx == arr.size()) {\n            res.insert(current_sum % mod);\n        } else {\n            dfs(idx + 1, (current_sum + arr[idx]) % mod);\n            dfs(idx + 1, current_sum);\n        }\n    };\n    \n    dfs(0, 0);\n    return res;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n, m;\n    cin >> n >> m;\n    \n    vector<int> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        cin >> a[i];\n        a[i] = a[i] % m;\n    }\n    \n    int half = n / 2;\n    set<int> left_sums = generate_subseq_sums(vector<int>(a.begin(), a.begin() + half), m);\n    set<int> right_sums_set = generate_subseq_sums(vector<int>(a.begin() + half, a.end()), m);\n    \n    vector<int> right_sorted(right_sums_set.begin(), right_sums_set.end());\n    sort(right_sorted.begin(), right_sorted.end());\n    \n    int max_val = 0;\n    for (int s : left_sums) {\n        int target = m - s;\n        auto idx = lower_bound(right_sorted.begin(), right_sorted.end(), target);\n        \n        if (idx != right_sorted.begin()) {\n            int candidate = s + *(idx - 1);\n            if (candidate > max_val) {\n                max_val = candidate;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        if (idx != right_sorted.end()) {\n            int candidate = s + *idx;\n            if (candidate > max_val) {\n                max_val = candidate;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    cout << max_val << endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00013958434283267707, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.0003625689132604748, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -4.756337511935271e-05, -5.960462772236497e-07, -2.74180